<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tours</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/732">732 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-invasion-of-gaul">Umayyad invasion of Gaul</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a>, also called the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a>, was fought in 732 CE in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, where Frankish forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> defeated an Umayyad army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-al-ghafiqi">Abd al-Rahman al-Ghafiqi</a>. It halted the northward advance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>. The victory greatly increased the power of Charles Martel and laid foundations for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tours.jpg" alt="Battle of Tours" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles de Steuben · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Steuben_-_Bataille_de_Poitiers.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
